  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Stonex Financial has $1.3B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date, from 355 awards with an average award size of $3.6M. Obligations are down 2.9% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations have varied: FY21 was $1.1B, FY22 was $1.7B, FY23 was $1.7B, FY24 was $703M, FY25 was $1.3B, and FY26 is $1.3B. The current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date, and the note clarifies that the listed award values in some tables represent total contract values rather than current-year obligations. This profile shows that Stonex Financial returned to a FY25 and FY26 level of $1.3B after a low point of $703M in FY24. The company received a relatively large number of awards for the obligation total, averaging $3.6M per award, which helps explain how the FY2026 to date obligations reached $1.3B across 355 actions.",
